/target
**/*.rs.bk

# Source papers stay local. Papers/README.md carries the full citations and
# links, so the repo stays small and redistribution of the PDFs is not this
# project's call to make.
Papers/*.pdf

# Benchmark datasets are large and externally hosted; fetch scripts live in
# benchmark/datasets/ instead.
benchmark/datasets/*
!benchmark/datasets/*.sh
!benchmark/datasets/*.md

# Engine data directories produced by tests and benchmark runs.
/data
*.sst
*.wal

# Raw benchmark output; committed results live in results/ as CSV + notebooks.
/results/raw

.ipynb_checkpoints/
__pycache__/
.venv/

# Claude Code local state. All of it is machine-specific: the settings file
# holds a permission allowlist naming local absolute paths, and the transient
# .tmp.* writes are occasionally caught mid-write by a "git add -A".
#
# A project that wanted to share Claude configuration with contributors would
# check in .claude/settings.json (shared) and .mcp.json (project MCP servers)
# while ignoring settings.local.json. Nothing here needs that, so the whole
# directory is ignored.
.claude/
CLAUDE.local.md

# Claude Code writes plans and transcripts under the user's home directory
# rather than the repo, so nothing else needs excluding.
